      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface biotinylation confirmed: KV10.1-AP was biotinylated at the cell surface by co-expressed BirA, demonstrating extracellular accessibility of the tag on the full-length, membrane-anchored channel. Electrophysiological function of the tagged channel was not reported in this clip.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "KV10.1 is KCNH1 (hEag1, UniProt Q12791); the ledger line explicitly states the AP tag was inserted 'after residue E317'. Python confirms seq[316]='E' and seq[317]='V', placing the junction at 317|318 within the extracellular S3\u2013S4 loop (topology span 313\u2013345). The junction is 5 residues from the TM3 C-terminus (312) and 29 residues from the TM4 N-terminus (346), satisfying the \u22653-residue TM-clearance rule. The 33-residue loop provides ample room for the insert. Full-length KV10.1 (= KCNH1, same protein, UniProt Q12791) expressed in HEK293 cells; the 35-aa acceptor peptide for biotin ligase (AP) was inserted after residue E317, in the S3\u2013S4 extracellular loop, to produce KV10.1-AP for surface biotinylation.",
