  "literature_notes": "KV10.1, hEag1, and KCNH1 are all names for the same human protein (UniProt Q12791, 989 aa). All ledger lines from PMC3192180 and PMC3086910 are therefore direct (not indirect) evidence for KCNH1. The only extracellular surface site supported by the ledger is the S3\u2013S4 loop junction 317|318, evidenced by two independent tag modalities (AP tag, L6; BBS, L1/L5) from two independent publications. L8 (BBS between TM3 and TM4, PMC3531731) and L7 (AP between S3 and S4, PMC3086910) corroborate the same loop without adding a new junction. L9 (PMC3743135) confirms BTX labeling of KV10.1-BBS but is post-lysis, not strictly surface. The three extracellular spans are: S1\u2013S2 loop (240\u2013248, 9 aa, no ledger support for tag insertion), S3\u2013S4 loop (313\u2013345, 33 aa, two validated tags), and S5\u2013S6 loop (398\u2013477, 80 aa, no ledger support for tag insertion). The N-terminal EGFP fusion (L10/L11) and C-terminal mVenus fusion (L12) are both intracellular and are recorded in other_positions. The AP tag (35 aa) exceeds the 13\u201323 aa guideline but is a published tolerated insertion; the BBS core (13 aa) falls within the range.",
